Package: BalExMed
Type: Package
Title: Balance-based Mediation Analysis for Compositional Exposures
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jing", "Ma", email = "jingma@fredhutch.org",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayesian mediation analysis in which a compositional exposure,
    such as the relative abundances of microbial taxa, affects a continuous
    outcome directly and through a continuous mediator. The composition enters
    the model through a latent balance, the normalized log-ratio between the
    geometric means of two unknown groups of parts. The two groups, the direct
    effect and the indirect effect are estimated jointly by a collapsed Gibbs
    sampler or a Metropolis-Hastings sampler, which return posterior inclusion
    probabilities for every part together with posterior draws of the effects.
